  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>gadopiclenol</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>V08CA12</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, IV dosing <small>(PK_1C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Eto T et al. 2025</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>Japanese and non-Japanese subjects, including adults and pediatric patients</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>gadopiclenol</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_gadopiclenol/Gadopiclenol_Eto2025_0_05_mmol_kg\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>Cmax (µg/mL)</td><td>524.5</td><td>µg/mL</td><td><small>Cmax</small></td></tr><tr><td>AUCinf (µg/mL.h)</td><td>569</td><td>µg/mL.h</td><td><small>AUC∞</small></td></tr><tr><td>AUCinf/Dose (µg/mL.h)</td><td>168</td><td>µg/mL.h</td><td><small>AUC/dose</small></td></tr><tr><td>t1/2 (h)</td><td>1.50</td><td>h</td><td><small>t1/2z</small></td></tr><tr><td>Vd (L)</td><td>13.0</td><td>L</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr><tr><td>Cl (L/h)</td><td>6.0</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>Clr (L/h)</td><td>5.2</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>CLR</small></td></tr><tr><td>fe (%)*</td><td>85.2</td><td></td><td><small>fe</small></td></tr></table><h4>About gadopiclenol</h4><p>Gadopiclenol is a gadolinium-based contrast agent used to improve images in magnetic resonance imaging. It is authorised in the European Union and is a newer agent, so it is not yet widely used.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q114748523\">Wikidata Q114748523</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica:/